      "title": "Chemistry Nobel recognizes work on how molecules acquire a single handedness",
      "summary": "Henri B. Kagan and Kenso Soai won the 2026 Nobel Prize in Chemistry for discoveries involving autocatalysis and asymmetric synthesis. Their work helps explain how one molecular “hand” can become dominant—a property important in chemistry and drug development.",
      "why_it_matters": "Molecular handedness can affect how substances behave in living systems, so methods for controlling it matter to pharmaceutical chemistry as well as fundamental questions about the chemistry of life.",
