      "title": "Italian firms plan €1 billion network of 13 data centers",
      "summary": "Core Stack and Green Arrow Capital said they plan to invest more than €1 billion over four years to build 13 mid-sized data centers in Italy. The companies say the sites will use on-site renewable generation and an Italian supply chain; the first two are still awaiting permits.",
      "why_it_matters": "A distributed, mid-sized approach could shape where digital infrastructure is built and how it connects to local power systems and suppliers. The projects also highlight the practical trade-offs between AI and cloud demand, permitting, and energy sourcing.",
