      "queued_at": "2026-10-07T17:08:33.964Z",
      "title": "Arctic sea ice ties for the satellite record’s tenth-lowest September minimum",
      "summary": "NASA and the National Snow and Ice Data Center estimate Arctic sea ice covered 4.6 million square kilometers at its annual minimum on September 12, 2026, tying 2008, 2010 and 2025 for the tenth-lowest minimum in the satellite record. The area remains well below the long-term average despite a recent relative plateau.",
      "why_it_matters": "The long-term decline and shift toward thinner, younger ice affect Arctic ecosystems and the region’s climate dynamics. The annual minimum is a useful measure of the broader trend, rather than a standalone indicator of any single year’s conditions.",
      "butterfly_question": "How might a thinner, younger Arctic ice cover change the region’s ecosystems and climate feedbacks?",
